{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T06:42:33.847117Z","id":"7d14c47be47441366461c089e687060c0ff31a6bd5ff81ca0331893e10398358","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs:1112-1121, record 1e165437.\n\nSpec §9.3: 'Declining keeps the rows held; a later ask there makes a new request only after 10 minutes'. request_in applies the same quiet period to routing, so a sender pressing Send again right after the approver declined does not re-announce the request; the rows are held and the agent's placeholder reads as not asked. If the owner wants a deliberate re-send to ask at once, drop the check for Cause::Routing.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":1115},"end":{"line":1124},"content_hash":"cf9707d61e55687d29484ea3ec1da7a8faa513bbca583c591bf81438ce7a4e23"},"summary":"A routed send within ten minutes of a decline makes no request, though spec §9.3 names only ask","tags":["people","spec:9.3","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T06:42:33.847251Z","id":"8a3caa1a2b31206df4b9e2fcd4aeeec5d3bbec2409233834f38908165cd8049b","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs:1286-1306, record 9f25f03b.\n\nwithheld_in_thread counts the authors withheld from each comment body (the rows a take holds, spec M16). A thread whose comments the agent may see but whose anchor, clip or artifact title is another person's (spec §3.3 step 6) is delivered with those fields placeholdered and makes no request; the agent can ask for the artifact's content outside threads with ask {approval: {url_or_id}} (Store::ask_approval, withheld_outside_threads), which covers text fields, the current version, documents and assets, but not a thread's anchor.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":1289},"end":{"line":1309},"content_hash":"2db7bc0ea49daabf8d49defd3d54488b8041d0c22a95068bc6531cfc23d68cee"},"summary":"Routing asks only for the authors of comment bodies; a withheld anchor, clip, batch note or title makes no request","tags":["people","spec:9.2","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T06:42:33.847354Z","id":"f5e6d679cca3d21c3e10e685e119fc16035f6df0a9efe59454ec184a2d2fc8a7","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs:1898-1908, record bfa6b632.\n\nThe overflow marker (install row approval_overflow:<approver>) lists the [author, artifact, thread] places whose routed content request_in held without a request, past MAX_OPEN_REQUESTS (100) per approver or MAX_OPEN_PER_AUTHOR (20) per author. Only Store::decide_request rechecks them, dropping a place once its content is no longer held without a request (held_without_request: answered by an open or declined request, delivered, gone, or now visible). A withdrawal or an approval made outside a decision changes nothing until the next decision, so the banner can outlive what it counted.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":1901},"end":{"line":1911},"content_hash":"e605efbaa1b77ac65394cb92bbe3b8380e6925c8a3c4e43692703b6852ef04e5"},"summary":"People's overflow banner stays up after withdrawals bring an approver under the limit, until their next decision","tags":["people","spec:9.2","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/exec.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T06:42:33.847433Z","id":"a1abac78188a15fada17e8991dd6ffd8caa0a07b79a872f0dcc758d68deac4bb","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/exec.rs:66-89, record c1fa8f66.\n\nSeen in Linux perf runs: a single commit held up by the disk. The writer runs WAL with SQLite's default synchronous=FULL, so every commit syncs the WAL, and the background PASSIVE checkpoint runs every CHECKPOINT_INTERVAL (2 s). Every delivery of a write waits on its commit, so one slow commit moves a whole cluster of deliveries (scripts/perf-clients.py:23-29 explains how the realtime gate copes).","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":66},"end":{"line":89},"content_hash":"19a1b1cc49fe118705a9d82f6b9227495d66a06ae11378ed14f24dfb809e7ed5"},"suggested_fix":"Measure commit times on Linux with synchronous=NORMAL (durable across a crash of the process, not of the machine, in WAL mode) and with a different checkpoint cadence before choosing.","summary":"On Linux, store commits occasionally take 25 to 120 ms","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T06:42:33.847604Z","id":"073e451c65608b6f5b4047ccf192d8da28e18918ae48c32153a1a83ca952f123","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs:1279-1291, record ed625c0d.\n\nEvery take runs Sight::row on each of its session's held rows again (thread_in, the comment's authors through the view), about 13 us a row measured at 09672011, before 7c10f0c1 indexed the request reads a held row's placeholder makes. A held row's hold changes only with the visibility generation (approvals, rights, people, claims) or when its row leaves the pending query (resolve, delete, delivery), so an in-memory map per session of (generation, held feedback IDs) would let a take skip each told held row while the generation is unchanged; the generation lives in memory, so the map must too. Not taken: with 7c10f0c1 and 7fd02f8a the perf gate's vis_feedback_poll_ms read 1.46, 1.54 and 1.51 ms per round in its quietest run (limit 1.78 ms), and with b24b98e0 as well 1.53 ms in its quietest round (load about 10 on 12 cores); scripts/perf-daemon.py withdraws the held rows after each poll, so a pile of held rows is not what it times.","kind":"alternative","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":1279},"end":{"line":1291},"content_hash":"14c749a089841625f0826ad94ddf4b36ba6e7b36afb83b6dd89c5d4a1f555b3f"},"summary":"Skip a take's told held rows while the visibility generation they were last found held at holds","tags":["revisit:vis_feedback_poll_ms over its limit again, or an agent's poll slowed by held rows its person leaves undecided","perf","visibility","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T06:42:33.847748Z","id":"bb87a56015c2add1c96c4b87f00787f57dcd46f4118450c3e4d4f181d964846d","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs:2116-2123, record 4efdda9a.\n\nDelivery::changed_for tells a person of a change only when their rows' newest time (StateRow::stamp: created, delivered, acknowledged, told, untargeted, last sent, session end) is the thread's newest. A change that sets no time (a watch armed or disarmed, which changes a sent row's waiting tier; a codex queue failure; a handoff that keeps a row's times) is published to the owner but to no person, so a connected person's open card keeps the old tier until the thread is fetched again. The owner hears every change.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":2116},"end":{"line":2123},"content_hash":"ae60d870fe573bb59b841ba7c4a344861a791c29f05330219c9330e9d6ad8e3e"},"summary":"A change that stamps no row reaches only the owner live; a person sees it at their next fetch","tags":["people","spec:10","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T06:42:33.847874Z","id":"7ce30a8b3a9dc706c6b8cc5cc5692b1544d13e4aee185a95e812462cedc4aafe","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs:2160-2169, record ddeebf95.\n\nstate_of reports withheld (the target session's person as approver) from placeholder_at, which a take sets when it holds and tells a row, or while an open approval request of that person covers the row's comment author there (a send naming the agent, spec §10). A comment that joins no request (a send naming no agent, a later reply whose author has no open request there, an author held past the request limits) reads sent, waiting on its tier, until the agent's next take. Computing it from visibility at state time would build a Visibility per target session's person inside feedback_states_in, which listings call for every thread (spec §8.7 cost).","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":2160},"end":{"line":2169},"content_hash":"00e0bbcb6caac54ad3191169bbd4afe7db0534f84731d8080a14ad9755c4d0d0"},"summary":"A held row that no open request covers reads sent until a take holds it","tags":["people","spec:8.4","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T06:42:33.848008Z","id":"9facff47b5fff8e74f47ea46f477bfb141db7978ee7435f1056cbc8334f089e0","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/inbox.rs:1363-1368, record 0118687f.\n\nconnection_decided reads a connection item only when the owner approves or denies the request (crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs approve_grant, deny_grant). A pending request that expires after 10 minutes (request_grant's stale sweep, expire_grants) leaves its item unread in the owner's inbox; once the unapproved row is purged a day later the item renders gone with connection null. Reading it at the lapse, or touching it so the shell shows the expired status, would need the lapse paths to call into the inbox.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":1363},"end":{"line":1368},"content_hash":"c1c86e26871ba066020c75f1d9b1b954ee91add027a8fb30f98694a07930d59d"},"summary":"A connection request that lapses unanswered keeps its connection item unread","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T06:42:33.848119Z","id":"d9ae8606a1af43bd153efdc4cdfbd410db028cdbd8c65eca4a519b1d26dda71b","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/inbox.rs:1552-1556, record 6014047e.\n\nnote_finished makes the finished item for the session's person. A first publish by a person's agent reaches both the person and the owner (note_version), since a new artifact appears in the owner's gallery; finished work was left to the person, per spec §18 ('Inbox, questions: own').","kind":"alternative","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":1552},"end":{"line":1556},"content_hash":"df46c2781c4e06aa0fe53e6fadd564b9bcbcad9e060403b47de165ac7d60413a"},"summary":"A connected person's agent's finished work reaches its person only, not the owner","tags":["revisit:the owner asks to follow other people's agents' work in their inbox","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T06:42:33.848207Z","id":"0ddfa157f963e14b879eca8b8c8cca5f4f3506ec2999a9c377840ab6fbc6367e","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs:724-727, record 5367fcc4.\n\nFailure: a home at migration 25 where a person's agent asked a question (a dev home run on this branch) keeps that question's item with recipient NULL after 26, so it sits in the owner's inbox and crates/clax-server/src/inbox.rs render reads its question unscoped (st.question), showing the person's question and answers to the owner, while the person never gets the item. Main's homes hold no person sessions, so they are unaffected. Accepted: migrations 24-26 are unmerged (spec M27), so only a dev home run on this branch can hold such items; questions themselves get their person from their session (questions.person is filled in by the migration).","kind":"waiver","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":724},"end":{"line":727},"content_hash":"d6145a7e9021458c787c755d995bbac04faf22bddf368c6753393c86d9e097ab"},"summary":"Migration 26 leaves every existing inbox item the owner's, including question and finished items a connected person's agent made at schema 24-25","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T06:42:33.848361Z","id":"2c328526a81cda80fc952edde60d11804357d9dd5b920bee632c8eb27a4511b1","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs:1088-1102, record b5059e16.\n\nFor flow invite the grant's events carry grant_id and person but not invite_id, so the journal cannot join invite.create to the grant made from it except by person and time; invites.grant_id holds the link only while the row lives.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":1088},"end":{"line":1102},"content_hash":"5797052e7ab6d41d1c7e1138621f9475ea1bbb4d84154b5bc865aea2b46b476f"},"suggested_fix":"Add invite_id to grant.request (flow invite) and to audit spec section 6.13 and multi-person spec section 20.2.","summary":"An invite-flow grant.request and grant.approve do not name the invite they redeemed","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T06:42:33.848504Z","id":"5978aff9195dfb72a0d2532585acb7cfc49d84441f5befde8c01c885863a633f","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs:1477-1569, record fbaca2aa.\n\napprove_owner_on_connect is the single approval made without a browser (spec section 21 item 3, M15). It is bounded to the connect: once per grant, within OWNER_ANSWER_SECS (10 minutes) of the tokens' issue, never once the person has made or revoked any approval of the owner (409 owner_answered, so a revocation in People stands; 409 answer_closed after the window), replays refused by accept_t first. Only the continuation token says it, never the access token agents sign with (crates/clax-server/tests/api_grants.rs a_connected_machine_approves_the_owner_through_its_continuation), and clax connect refuses on an agent channel (crates/clax-cli/tests/connect.rs connect_refuses_on_an_agent_channel). What remains: a process of the person's that reads remote.json within those ten minutes, before clax connect answers, could answer yes for them; the person can revoke it in People, and that revocation is final. Tests: store::people::tests::connecting_records_the_persons_approval_of_the_owner_once, the_answer_about_the_owner_never_overrides_the_person.","kind":"waiver","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":1477},"end":{"line":1569},"content_hash":"5d260869dffa70dec7dfc40d7ad1104c236566f218f6537d20ff488531c27bd3"},"summary":"The person's approval of the owner is recorded without a browser once, at connect: an agent present then could answer for the person","tags":["security","spec:6.3","spec:21","M15","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T06:42:33.848631Z","id":"05ca3c90a72b9254238c8d4ff6ac2fdff13d731d1a21261c0e67eac9642a67cd","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs:2273-2301, record 1d272fa3.\n\nAn invite that expires unredeemed records nothing (audit spec section 6.13 lists only invite.create and invite.revoke). When release_unconnected then returns its person to a plain viewer it sets person = 0 and rights_json = NULL in the sweep or a revoke, so rights set by invite.create's rights or person.rights change with no person.rights event: the journal's last word on that person's rights is wrong.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":2273},"end":{"line":2301},"content_hash":"d242a9bd90c214f1d970d7480517326bcd61c2f544904cea6543d0a77c276506"},"summary":"An invite's lapse is not recorded, and release_unconnected clears a person's flag and rights without an event","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/sessions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T06:42:33.848766Z","id":"6146447fbc2c0620a01b1199ea38beec43fbf714e038bd0c6da07618a6f2da37","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs:213-219, record d9e10887.\n\nRegistration derives a name from the repository and branch (spec section 11) without an event; session.start's body is harness, harness_session_id, cwd, transcript_path and pid. The first agent.name then reports previous: <derived name> with no earlier event naming it, and an @name in a comment cannot be tied to its session from the journal alone.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":187},"end":{"line":193},"content_hash":"2531645c1bbef5581474f3318cd70a2a599ab739af3be8223fbe8da994159a5b"},"suggested_fix":"Add name (classed as a name for redaction) to session.start and session.join bodies, and say so in audit spec section 6.8.","summary":"A session's derived name is never recorded, so agent.name's previous names a value the journal never held","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/sessions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T06:42:33.848884Z","id":"905a0b004c57352857dfd4b94cc1178fd740114a79f658ed9292fe17c4b0c7b5","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs:1639-1655, record bcb6cc4e.\n\nrelease_owned_in (crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs) selects threads WHERE target_session_id = ?1, and Store::roster groups threads by target_session_id; crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs indexes neither. Both are full scans of threads: off the request hot paths (ends, the reaper, GET /api/agents) and cheap at today's sizes, but linear in all threads ever made.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":1615},"end":{"line":1631},"content_hash":"20c6bc83236711f3d0fd91be27eb8807d928e32beb5474638e9b1e8ace251388"},"suggested_fix":"Add CREATE INDEX threads_by_target ON threads(target_session_id) WHERE target_session_id IS NOT NULL in the next migration.","summary":"Every session end and every roster read scans threads for target_session_id, which has no index","tags":["perf","revisit:the next migration on this branch","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/sessions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T06:42:33.848990Z","id":"9daba4912ee6d6dfc47850bd226691e02de2be5246e18c7cabb1f19500a18299","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs:2264-2279, record 33053daa.\n\nFailure: at load average 38, `fresh` (registered after the 300 ms sleep) was more than 200 ms old when reap_sessions(200 ms) ran, so it was reaped too and reaped.ended.len() was 3, not 2. It passed when rerun alone. The test measures idleness by the wall clock (std::thread::sleep, then a fixed limit), which the repository's test rules (AGENTS.md, Code) reserve for injected clocks.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":2240},"end":{"line":2255},"content_hash":"16f02efa7807605004f5ea6b2d933316c5883e439d41718811276850897ae21a"},"suggested_fix":"Give reap_sessions the current time (or a Clock) so the test advances it instead of sleeping, and drop the sleep.","summary":"reaper_ends_only_idle_sessions_with_dead_or_unknown_pids sleeps against a 200 ms idle limit and fails on a loaded machine","tags":["flaky-test","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/viewers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T06:42:33.849063Z","id":"3cc636cad7aee26772279a44902fc1f8cd7f325b98733afa56e2c69bd3104f02","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/viewers.rs:64-84, record fd6040ef.\n\nAt 8446429: upsert_viewer(lan, 'Аlex') with no owner name succeeds; set_owner_name('Alex') then succeeds too, and both names stand. An agent registering from repository web is named 'web' beside a LAN viewer 'wеb'. New people are covered (check_person_name refuses a look-alike held by an uninvited viewer). The owner usually names themselves late, on a first comment, so pre-squatting is the likely order.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":64},"end":{"line":84},"content_hash":"24d54c01aee4c9c1101ef35072eaf1ae1b3afad2ce8cd4595110fe4e2fff2339"},"suggested_fix":"Mark it where names are shown: an unconnected viewer whose name looks like a protected name is flagged in the shell and in agent author lines (with spec section 9.6's '(not connected)', Task 17), rather than refusing the owner their own name.","summary":"The look-alike check runs only when the later name is set: a LAN viewer who took 'Аlex' before the owner named themselves 'Alex', or 'wеb' before an agent web went live, keeps it","tags":["review","spec:9.6","revisit:task-17","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/viewers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T06:42:33.849121Z","id":"bcc550ca536dc1431c1a6bcd1c499a6c025eee49e37da1cc520a7ff02c4534aa","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/viewers.rs:210-227, record 93ccd2dd.\n\nMigration 24 hashes every existing viewer's row ID into viewer_cookies with legacy = 1 so existing LAN viewers keep their identity; a legacy cookie never names a person (VIEWER_BY_COOKIE), a viewer made a person loses its legacy cookies (create_invite), and GET /api/viewers/me replaces one with a cxv_ secret (reissue_viewer_cookie). Until that call, someone who minted viewers in the same millisecond as the victim on main could still act as that anonymous viewer (comment, rename): the pre-branch exposure, now bounded to unvisited anonymous viewers. Retiring every legacy cookie at once (say, at the first daemon start after a fixed date) would close it at the cost of those viewers' identities.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":210},"end":{"line":227},"content_hash":"8299dae6a186c40de75360a6569a05295050802db3e965a3637151f5d3dafa4f"},"summary":"An anonymous LAN viewer migrated from main keeps its guessable legacy cookie (its row ID, a monotonic ULID) until that browser next calls GET /api/viewers/me","tags":["final-review","security","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/visibility.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T06:42:33.849211Z","id":"d76acb9a6d6838126227460d182c659b9b2ae8e3487345903fbc284155785243","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/visibility.rs:72-79, record 1ce70140.\n\nMoved from crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs:330-337, record b8541bce.\n\nUnattributed history is marked '(not connected)' (owner's decision on 7fdbaaf5). Comments the owner's browser made between migrations 12 and 15 carry a viewer row with minted_local NULL that claim_for_owner (crates/clax-core/src/store/viewers.rs) never claims, so they are marked on real installs too. Matching names is spoofable (spec §21.2); an explicit fold by the owner in the browser is not.","kind":"alternative","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":72},"end":{"line":79},"content_hash":"31b72a09f53496f8d927466a9d2f661853a503a3fd7274e62dbae25d003fa4ac"},"summary":"An owner-only, browser-only 'this was me' in People that folds a legacy viewer row (or claims unattributed comments) into the owner, unmarking that history without trusting names","tags":["revisit:owners report their own old comments marked as not connected","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T06:42:34.253650Z","id":"9609992cfacfb0909c6877b0dd17f600390c34801ba0ba94850d4a0689c678af","body":{"detail":"A watch armed or disarmed, a codex queue failure and a handoff that keeps times change only the tier text of a sent row ('waiting on the agent finishing its current work' and the like); every decision reaches its approver and author (publish_decision), so no person keeps a stale hold, decline or approval from these. Two gaps remain: (1) a comment a page wrote has several authors (page_authors), and a decision's parties name only the request's author, so the page's other authors read the row (Delivery::sees) but hear nothing of the decision until they fetch; code reading. (2) The hub's repeat suppression (crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs project, ch.delivery) remembers the last state sent per recipient key and channel, not what the client applied, so a reader whose client dropped a state (a new thread's state arriving before its thread event: record on crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs:539-573) or that fetched after an unsent change is not sent that state again.","kind":"comment","references":"bb87a56015c2add1c96c4b87f00787f57dcd46f4118450c3e4d4f181d964846d","summary":"Assessment: the unstamped changes only move a waiting tier, which misleads no one; two cases do leave a person reading a wrong state","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T06:42:34.253731Z","id":"7ae666526fca058994860b17b7fbca00a993b54e94b8ac0432fb4a95dbcde068","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"bb87a56015c2add1c96c4b87f00787f57dcd46f4118450c3e4d4f181d964846d","summary":"Two gaps reply 65115b61 named are closed in c84e0d7a: a decision now reaches the content's co-authors (Delivery::decision_people), and the hub forgets what it sent a person when a stream of theirs subscribes or resumes. The tier staleness this record describes stays.","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T06:42:34.259436Z","id":"aea335be81751f49cf5928738830faa80f488e565d2889cd4188bfafd542e55d","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"9facff47b5fff8e74f47ea46f477bfb141db7978ee7435f1056cbc8334f089e0","summary":"The owner can now mark such an item read from its card (ConnectionCard's Mark read, 2eb5ce4a); the lapse paths still leave it unread.","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T06:42:34.273108Z","id":"ffc35068018ff1039d4e56fda997acfa02742d7d40ae4e2983e4e10cd496a407","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"05ca3c90a72b9254238c8d4ff6ac2fdff13d731d1a21261c0e67eac9642a67cd","summary":"Partly addressed by 7329a263: a release now drops every raise the released person gave, each recorded as agent.elevate with reason person_released; the release itself (the person flag and rights cleared) is still not recorded.","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/viewers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T06:42:34.283946Z","id":"1583c185ad16ac1d755d35ea9b48346d49dd7f90ff2e4a7e766f28caf23f774c","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"3cc636cad7aee26772279a44902fc1f8cd7f325b98733afa56e2c69bd3104f02","summary":"The agent side of the suggested fix landed in 7e11f344 and 35cec880: every name of a viewer who is neither the owner nor a person reads '<name> (not connected)' in what an agent gets (feedback items and their author lines, batch senders, withheld authors, thread comments, resolved_by_name, artifact participants; crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs Connected::label, crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs mark_thread). A LAN viewer named 'Аlex' therefore reads 'Аlex (not connected)' to the owner's agents (api_people::unconnected_authors_are_marked_not_connected). The shell's flag for such a viewer is still open, for the People and thread-card UI.","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T13:02:15.482258Z","id":"4616e47c7730423a92ba80cfdb72d0a378d7f88c795bc7dffe8eef7e210b4b97","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs:1112-1121, record 1e165437.\n\nSpec §9.3: 'Declining keeps the rows held; a later ask there makes a new request only after 10 minutes'. request_in applies the same quiet period to routing, so a sender pressing Send again right after the approver declined does not re-announce the request; the rows are held and the agent's placeholder reads as not asked. If the owner wants a deliberate re-send to ask at once, drop the check for Cause::Routing.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:3cadd457","span":{"start":{"line":1116},"end":{"line":1125},"content_hash":"cf9707d61e55687d29484ea3ec1da7a8faa513bbca583c591bf81438ce7a4e23"},"summary":"A routed send within ten minutes of a decline makes no request, though spec §9.3 names only ask","supersedes":"7d14c47be47441366461c089e687060c0ff31a6bd5ff81ca0331893e10398358","tags":["people","spec:9.3","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T13:02:15.485353Z","id":"897cdd91477c74122263714ef2c09ba64db264aead09f8a3f284c3108184f372","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs:1286-1306, record 9f25f03b.\n\nwithheld_in_thread counts the authors withheld from each comment body (the rows a take holds, spec M16). A thread whose comments the agent may see but whose anchor, clip or artifact title is another person's (spec §3.3 step 6) is delivered with those fields placeholdered and makes no request; the agent can ask for the artifact's content outside threads with ask {approval: {url_or_id}} (Store::ask_approval, withheld_outside_threads), which covers text fields, the current version, documents and assets, but not a thread's anchor.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:3cadd457","span":{"start":{"line":1290},"end":{"line":1310},"content_hash":"2db7bc0ea49daabf8d49defd3d54488b8041d0c22a95068bc6531cfc23d68cee"},"summary":"Routing asks only for the authors of comment bodies; a withheld anchor, clip, batch note or title makes no request","supersedes":"8a3caa1a2b31206df4b9e2fcd4aeeec5d3bbec2409233834f38908165cd8049b","tags":["people","spec:9.2","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T13:02:15.488362Z","id":"4e99c5ba140ed3ad4f2089b684fe49bc976fbac2289c291158be039169f4c186","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs:1898-1908, record bfa6b632.\n\nThe overflow marker (install row approval_overflow:<approver>) lists the [author, artifact, thread] places whose routed content request_in held without a request, past MAX_OPEN_REQUESTS (100) per approver or MAX_OPEN_PER_AUTHOR (20) per author. Only Store::decide_request rechecks them, dropping a place once its content is no longer held without a request (held_without_request: answered by an open or declined request, delivered, gone, or now visible). A withdrawal or an approval made outside a decision changes nothing until the next decision, so the banner can outlive what it counted.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:3cadd457","span":{"start":{"line":1902},"end":{"line":1912},"content_hash":"e605efbaa1b77ac65394cb92bbe3b8380e6925c8a3c4e43692703b6852ef04e5"},"summary":"People's overflow banner stays up after withdrawals bring an approver under the limit, until their next decision","supersedes":"f5e6d679cca3d21c3e10e685e119fc16035f6df0a9efe59454ec184a2d2fc8a7","tags":["people","spec:9.2","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T13:02:15.491424Z","id":"d68ad38cfb2a5e9f9c792b059399d23deaacc0d04fa0dfb07d17f29045af3b09","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs:1279-1291, record ed625c0d.\n\nEvery take runs Sight::row on each of its session's held rows again (thread_in, the comment's authors through the view), about 13 us a row measured at 09672011, before 7c10f0c1 indexed the request reads a held row's placeholder makes. A held row's hold changes only with the visibility generation (approvals, rights, people, claims) or when its row leaves the pending query (resolve, delete, delivery), so an in-memory map per session of (generation, held feedback IDs) would let a take skip each told held row while the generation is unchanged; the generation lives in memory, so the map must too. Not taken: with 7c10f0c1 and 7fd02f8a the perf gate's vis_feedback_poll_ms read 1.46, 1.54 and 1.51 ms per round in its quietest run (limit 1.78 ms), and with b24b98e0 as well 1.53 ms in its quietest round (load about 10 on 12 cores); scripts/perf-daemon.py withdraws the held rows after each poll, so a pile of held rows is not what it times.","kind":"alternative","ref":"git:3cadd457","span":{"start":{"line":1280},"end":{"line":1292},"content_hash":"14c749a089841625f0826ad94ddf4b36ba6e7b36afb83b6dd89c5d4a1f555b3f"},"summary":"Skip a take's told held rows while the visibility generation they were last found held at holds","supersedes":"073e451c65608b6f5b4047ccf192d8da28e18918ae48c32153a1a83ca952f123","tags":["revisit:vis_feedback_poll_ms over its limit again, or an agent's poll slowed by held rows its person leaves undecided","perf","visibility","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T13:02:15.494416Z","id":"ff9f942a8c9b632eb661afb4b27fd0b47f8b567b53e3e114d974be830f7c16b9","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs:2116-2123, record 4efdda9a.\n\nDelivery::changed_for tells a person of a change only when their rows' newest time (StateRow::stamp: created, delivered, acknowledged, told, untargeted, last sent, session end) is the thread's newest. A change that sets no time (a watch armed or disarmed, which changes a sent row's waiting tier; a codex queue failure; a handoff that keeps a row's times) is published to the owner but to no person, so a connected person's open card keeps the old tier until the thread is fetched again. The owner hears every change.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:3cadd457","span":{"start":{"line":2117},"end":{"line":2124},"content_hash":"ae60d870fe573bb59b841ba7c4a344861a791c29f05330219c9330e9d6ad8e3e"},"summary":"A change that stamps no row reaches only the owner live; a person sees it at their next fetch","supersedes":"bb87a56015c2add1c96c4b87f00787f57dcd46f4118450c3e4d4f181d964846d","tags":["people","spec:10","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T13:02:15.497407Z","id":"13d79c95856a48d0f4b710db96131c6ca4fe3f99af74dca5dd3c6760b127dcc1","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs:2160-2169, record ddeebf95.\n\nstate_of reports withheld (the target session's person as approver) from placeholder_at, which a take sets when it holds and tells a row, or while an open approval request of that person covers the row's comment author there (a send naming the agent, spec §10). A comment that joins no request (a send naming no agent, a later reply whose author has no open request there, an author held past the request limits) reads sent, waiting on its tier, until the agent's next take. Computing it from visibility at state time would build a Visibility per target session's person inside feedback_states_in, which listings call for every thread (spec §8.7 cost).","kind":"concern","ref":"git:3cadd457","span":{"start":{"line":2161},"end":{"line":2170},"content_hash":"00e0bbcb6caac54ad3191169bbd4afe7db0534f84731d8080a14ad9755c4d0d0"},"summary":"A held row that no open request covers reads sent until a take holds it","supersedes":"7ce30a8b3a9dc706c6b8cc5cc5692b1544d13e4aee185a95e812462cedc4aafe","tags":["people","spec:8.4","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/visibility.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T13:02:15.500366Z","id":"ec1b4b8cc08564396ec254194f7a05b9f7ec44518e4cedb2e7fe49dd642057b5","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/visibility.rs:72-79, record 1ce70140.\n\nMoved from crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs:330-337, record b8541bce.\n\nUnattributed history is marked '(not connected)' (owner's decision on 7fdbaaf5). Comments the owner's browser made between migrations 12 and 15 carry a viewer row with minted_local NULL that claim_for_owner (crates/clax-core/src/store/viewers.rs) never claims, so they are marked on real installs too. Matching names is spoofable (spec §21.2); an explicit fold by the owner in the browser is not.","kind":"alternative","ref":"git:3cadd457","span":{"start":{"line":71},"end":{"line":78},"content_hash":"31b72a09f53496f8d927466a9d2f661853a503a3fd7274e62dbae25d003fa4ac"},"summary":"An owner-only, browser-only 'this was me' in People that folds a legacy viewer row (or claims unattributed comments) into the owner, unmarking that history without trusting names","supersedes":"d76acb9a6d6838126227460d182c659b9b2ae8e3487345903fbc284155785243","tags":["revisit:owners report their own old comments marked as not connected","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.991853Z","id":"b23d27927920957c602bd80775abd1f7645a73edf7d6f98467712fc087cb578e","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs:1128-1137, record 5df9c893.\n\nSpec §9.3: 'Declining keeps the rows held; a later ask there makes a new request only after 10 minutes'. request_in applies the same quiet period to routing, so a sender pressing Send again right after the approver declined does not re-announce the request; the rows are held and the agent's placeholder reads as not asked. If the owner wants a deliberate re-send to ask at once, drop the check for Cause::Routing.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":1126},"end":{"line":1135},"content_hash":"cf9707d61e55687d29484ea3ec1da7a8faa513bbca583c591bf81438ce7a4e23"},"summary":"A routed send within ten minutes of a decline makes no request, though spec §9.3 names only ask","tags":["people","spec:9.3","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.991986Z","id":"db8994c4dd781f86cd721da7d7f14525e1bdc25f02abae98c46b0d96a2187f95","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs:1302-1322, record ffffcf0f.\n\nwithheld_in_thread counts the authors withheld from each comment body (the rows a take holds, spec M16). A thread whose comments the agent may see but whose anchor, clip or artifact title is another person's (spec §3.3 step 6) is delivered with those fields placeholdered and makes no request; the agent can ask for the artifact's content outside threads with ask {approval: {url_or_id}} (Store::ask_approval, withheld_outside_threads), which covers text fields, the current version, documents and assets, but not a thread's anchor.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":1300},"end":{"line":1320},"content_hash":"2db7bc0ea49daabf8d49defd3d54488b8041d0c22a95068bc6531cfc23d68cee"},"summary":"Routing asks only for the authors of comment bodies; a withheld anchor, clip, batch note or title makes no request","tags":["people","spec:9.2","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.992085Z","id":"58a168b354ac59dd7fd0e933ae2ae927dd27733d09315ff5d8b23c150031374a","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs:1914-1924, record 232ba483.\n\nThe overflow marker (install row approval_overflow:<approver>) lists the [author, artifact, thread] places whose routed content request_in held without a request, past MAX_OPEN_REQUESTS (100) per approver or MAX_OPEN_PER_AUTHOR (20) per author. Only Store::decide_request rechecks them, dropping a place once its content is no longer held without a request (held_without_request: answered by an open or declined request, delivered, gone, or now visible). A withdrawal or an approval made outside a decision changes nothing until the next decision, so the banner can outlive what it counted.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":1912},"end":{"line":1922},"content_hash":"e605efbaa1b77ac65394cb92bbe3b8380e6925c8a3c4e43692703b6852ef04e5"},"summary":"People's overflow banner stays up after withdrawals bring an approver under the limit, until their next decision","tags":["people","spec:9.2","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.992438Z","id":"6dbd24d8ca07de749b55acdb966d0f733668729ba077d8793a3208070c02dafe","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs:1154-1174, record f6358543.\n\nA push to Cloudflare Artifacts whose pushed event is lost, late or never delivered (no subscription, locally: the queue is simulated and receives none, crates/clax-worker/wrangler.jsonc queues) stays unrecorded until the next publish of the artifact, so viewers see the older version meanwhile. The prototype also reconciles lazily on reads, at most every RECONCILE_EVERY_MS (hosted/src/do/artifact.ts reconcileLazily). Fix: reconcile from the artifact read routes when main has moved past the current version's commit, rate-limited per artifact.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":1151},"end":{"line":1171},"content_hash":"5aea8e38f17328396770571e0e3d99efadde21ae073543404d5fa024591c706c"},"summary":"Pushed commits are recorded on a push, an Artifacts event or a publish, but not when an artifact is read","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.992527Z","id":"b3ddffd255fec19e18df53ad65cf1e950d390c7ae90d58dd8a2a17e1c9e1a351","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs:1246-1268, record 8c8d734d.\n\nrecord_version_locked calls revoke_blind_tokens with the publisher for VersionStep::Write when expected > 0, which is ContentStore::repo_tokens (DoLedger: POST token/live to RepoDO) even when no token is held. That is one subrequest on every publish's path (time to usable), plus a Visibility per agent token. Skipping needs to know no agent token is live without asking RepoDO, for example a held-token count the instance keeps from mint and revoke answers.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":1243},"end":{"line":1265},"content_hash":"a791ca23cf8107bccfd6950065f7527248cabd7d27c31964f2e4f1eeeeb672b6"},"summary":"Every publish of an existing artifact asks the push ledger for the repository's tokens before its commit: on the Worker one RepoDO call per publish","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.992607Z","id":"df2d0cb05a2220e63b4c9b7580be5a967e85a24c8367324213a738e89b82e06d","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs:1284-1293, record bd81b2ff.\n\nArtifactLocks (content/mod.rs) serialise version writes within one process, so there the loser waits and then sees Conflict (concurrent_publishes_with_same_if_version_yield_one_winner). Across processes the loser's content write fails first; it is mapped to Conflict only when the artifact has already moved past the expected version. Nothing is corrupted (the loser removes nothing it did not write). The daemon is the only writer of versions today.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":1281},"end":{"line":1290},"content_hash":"4904f3490dcc2f9f92baa1aaa49032071480c9eaf3740604defd236f4657e508"},"summary":"Two processes publishing the same version at once: the loser gets the content store's AlreadyExists error, not Conflict, while the winner has not yet recorded it","tags":["content-store","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.992685Z","id":"98301473f1f373e458193db70f6a438e1b18328b2aee02d82f711e3b7a2b5cc0","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs:1415-1432, record 7e511288.\n\nStore::version_meta resolves p.person, else the session's person, else the owner, before the content write; version_authors (artifacts.rs:817) resolves the row's person again inside the transaction. They agree today (tests a_version_write_names_its_publisher_agent_and_note), but a change to one rule that misses the other makes git's Clax-Publisher disagree with the row.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":1412},"end":{"line":1429},"content_hash":"48d111421f495d2e72c03035f37a629a7bd29de6662dec8fbd17c5f02aa85418"},"suggested_fix":"Resolve the person once before the content lock and pass it to version_authors.","summary":"The publisher the content store is told and the one the version row records are resolved by separate code","tags":["review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/device.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.993016Z","id":"ff76d808fc22ebfaec9c930a42cdff9c5e95df6d33b52695cd704b679f952756","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/device.rs:183-209, record 4e3bca1d.\n\napprove_device mints the bearer grant at approval; the token is only issued at the next poll, and the code expires after 600 s. Nobody holds the token, but the grant stays listed until revoked by hand.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:69750b2990275429f946bb32d6d188b3e9d50145","span":{"start":{"line":183},"end":{"line":209},"content_hash":"ce7e08161692dd5ed330e4a1c699eaaa3595d06aa0ec20426b822b2f2a187a6b"},"summary":"A device sign-in approved but never polled (the machine went away) leaves a live agent token on its person's People page","tags":["security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/exec.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.993362Z","id":"b5db32547cbb40c2846a077b2cbd293fd03c388f6e1132fc73ac52b07ab91455","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/exec.rs:246-269, record fbfa68ba.\n\nSeen in Linux perf runs: a single commit held up by the disk. The writer runs WAL with SQLite's default synchronous=FULL, so every commit syncs the WAL, and the background PASSIVE checkpoint runs every CHECKPOINT_INTERVAL (2 s). Every delivery of a write waits on its commit, so one slow commit moves a whole cluster of deliveries (scripts/perf-clients.py:23-29 explains how the realtime gate copes).","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":246},"end":{"line":269},"content_hash":"19a1b1cc49fe118705a9d82f6b9227495d66a06ae11378ed14f24dfb809e7ed5"},"suggested_fix":"Measure commit times on Linux with synchronous=NORMAL (durable across a crash of the process, not of the machine, in WAL mode) and with a different checkpoint cadence before choosing.","summary":"On Linux, store commits occasionally take 25 to 120 ms","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/exec.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.993442Z","id":"dc11e4cdbdc735c4d574637cc64a5f799ecfc7ea0f263334669692e4c646eb7f","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/exec.rs:916-946, record 7600eccb.\n\nOn the pool a started job runs to completion on its worker (call_on_worker), but inline the request future owns the job: a client gone or a timeout layer dropping the handler between ContentStore::write_version and the version transaction (store/artifacts.rs:1145) skips both the record and the remove_version that a failed transaction runs. FsContent and a create-only git backend then refuse version n as already present (artifacts.rs a_stray_version_directory_refuses_the_publish_and_records_nothing), so the artifact cannot be published again until the stray is removed (clax doctor natively; nothing on a Durable Object). A dropped clipped thread creation leaves an unreferenced clip; a dropped create_artifact a zero-version row. Removing an unrecorded n before writing it is safe only where one process writes the content (a Durable Object), not natively with several daemons (record 4f959f4e).","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":916},"end":{"line":946},"content_hash":"68f7616e26a49e70da13008ab0b933c12adca6dea763e30fb402f4ea0f4602dd"},"suggested_fix":"On one connection, make an unrecorded version n replaceable: when write_version reports n present and the row still says n - 1, remove_version(n) under the content lock and write again; or run the job to completion detached from the request (ctx.waitUntil on a Worker).","summary":"A call_async job awaited inline (one connection, wasm32) stops wherever its future is dropped, so a cancelled publish can leave version n written but unrecorded, which refuses every later publish of n","tags":["content-store","wasm","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.993857Z","id":"ee6be998e9f69f7a705db626f089a9e0e936bb2574ec8d271cbc89041e19f9ed","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs:1286-1298, record 58db64c5.\n\nEvery take runs Sight::row on each of its session's held rows again (thread_in, the comment's authors through the view), about 13 us a row measured at 09672011, before 7c10f0c1 indexed the request reads a held row's placeholder makes. A held row's hold changes only with the visibility generation (approvals, rights, people, claims) or when its row leaves the pending query (resolve, delete, delivery), so an in-memory map per session of (generation, held feedback IDs) would let a take skip each told held row while the generation is unchanged; the generation lives in memory, so the map must too. Not taken: with 7c10f0c1 and 7fd02f8a the perf gate's vis_feedback_poll_ms read 1.46, 1.54 and 1.51 ms per round in its quietest run (limit 1.78 ms), and with b24b98e0 as well 1.53 ms in its quietest round (load about 10 on 12 cores); scripts/perf-daemon.py withdraws the held rows after each poll, so a pile of held rows is not what it times.","kind":"alternative","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":1287},"end":{"line":1299},"content_hash":"014f358e63a6a09fa987dc7c09362de304393d1a90fd4797054e615bc5e0dac1"},"summary":"Skip a take's told held rows while the visibility generation they were last found held at holds","tags":["revisit:vis_feedback_poll_ms over its limit again, or an agent's poll slowed by held rows its person leaves undecided","perf","visibility","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.994029Z","id":"2bb2a20501aa96b3d24691a54b758269a798de3a5dddf58830ca8827f4bcde57","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs:1347-1350, record 9e8e75ed.\n\nfeedback.rs:1266 and clax-server/src/feedback.rs snapshot_path name versions/<n>/index.html under the home; thread clips (Home::clip_path, site.rs refile) stay files; backfill.rs hashes version files and assets on disk; stray_version_dirs (artifacts.rs:498), stray_asset_temp_files (assets.rs:350), AssetRow::path and clax doctor's version_files check read the FsContent layout. All are correct only for a store whose content is the home's files (the default).","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":1348},"end":{"line":1351},"content_hash":"5f14d50338b191def62d9993b2d831fed5f0e478d291d4c8473e8312b17cf7c8"},"summary":"Several paths still use the home's files directly, outside ContentStore: snapshot paths handed to agents, clip images, the audit backfill, and doctor's stray scans","tags":["content-store","wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.994365Z","id":"4d2b858384a4a0293cc04b0b134dc2465286797341ec5a926cd75d215550866e","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs:2136-2143, record d3cc1f6f.\n\nDelivery::changed_for tells a person of a change only when their rows' newest time (StateRow::stamp: created, delivered, acknowledged, told, untargeted, last sent, session end) is the thread's newest. A change that sets no time (a watch armed or disarmed, which changes a sent row's waiting tier; a codex queue failure; a handoff that keeps a row's times) is published to the owner but to no person, so a connected person's open card keeps the old tier until the thread is fetched again. The owner hears every change.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":2137},"end":{"line":2144},"content_hash":"a0352ae277d3e1bd4888457d701a8ee4f88820b6751df49739bcfa70ab5c97a5"},"summary":"A change that stamps no row reaches only the owner live; a person sees it at their next fetch","tags":["people","spec:10","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.994485Z","id":"d7231b246431eb9f7e68fee1e4fa1ddc6cbee574e227bef9211f80113e634c7c","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs:2180-2189, record b3d6f93e.\n\nstate_of reports withheld (the target session's person as approver) from placeholder_at, which a take sets when it holds and tells a row, or while an open approval request of that person covers the row's comment author there (a send naming the agent, spec §10). A comment that joins no request (a send naming no agent, a later reply whose author has no open request there, an author held past the request limits) reads sent, waiting on its tier, until the agent's next take. Computing it from visibility at state time would build a Visibility per target session's person inside feedback_states_in, which listings call for every thread (spec §8.7 cost).","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":2181},"end":{"line":2190},"content_hash":"c65b0f968699e8cc0c38af1592e8e7b90d060df9c18a71599f611feba41154f4"},"summary":"A held row that no open request covers reads sent until a take holds it","tags":["people","spec:8.4","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/forks.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.994721Z","id":"7a64361dfb8f3d6d4d130bbdd95fdcae6f1b6ba7c5cb5bcb0ad93b55649cb8a4","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/forks.rs:1-4, record 859ed4c3.\n\nhosted/src/do/artifact.ts keeps a forks table on the original and broadcasts a fork event; spec 2026-10-11-clax-dev-hosted-design H11 says the original lists its forks. Here only the fork records its source (artifacts.forked_from_id); listing a source's forks is a query on that column (no index yet) plus a filtered view.","kind":"alternative","ref":"git:69966ab214615ef0117a4fd6fd79db8dc25937d3","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":4},"content_hash":"34369e2e065901c8e4d6445f8a060034bbe43fae44330b7c5bc627d18c54d5b4"},"summary":"The source does not list its forks (the hosted prototype's Forks (n) and fork live events)","tags":["forks","revisit:when the artifact view gets a forks list","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/forks.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.994773Z","id":"3f605810ac353760dd7f00a5dd173cad7dd7b7ebf066e5a9b7718bb25f2a5aa8","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/forks.rs:13-14, record cbd48570.\n\nStore::fork_artifact_async copies version files only (ContentStore::fork). Pages reference assets by ID alone: the upload answers /_blob/<asset ID> (a hosted daemon's /_blob/<asset ID>?k=<key>, keyed by the asset ID only, hosted.rs asset_url), and routes/assets.rs blob looks the row up by ID (Store::get_asset). So the fork's page keeps loading the source's assets for every reader of the fork, a hosted one too (the key is in the page's bytes), until the source is deleted (delete_artifact_async removes its content, assets included) or its owner deletes that asset; the fork's own asset list (GET /api/artifacts/<fork>/assets) is empty. Copying under the same IDs is impossible: assets.id is the table's primary key (migration 1) and /_blob/<id> names no artifact. Copying under new IDs means rewriting the copied files' bytes, which changes the hashes and authors' bytes the fork keeps (content_sha256 equal to the source version's, crates/clax-core/src/store/forks.rs tests) and misses URLs a page builds in script. The hosted prototype has no assets.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:69966ab214615ef0117a4fd6fd79db8dc25937d3","span":{"start":{"line":13},"end":{"line":14},"content_hash":"f58f8d887d87cc58a86164f841f02fa75222496da147750b95e672cbb1a45d68"},"suggested_fix":"Decide: (a) key assets by (artifact_id, id) with /_blob/<id> resolved within the page's artifact (a migration and a route that knows its artifact), then copy rows and bytes under the same IDs into the fork; (b) keep a deleted artifact's asset bytes while a live fork names it as its source; or (c) accept, and say in docs/contract.md's fork section that assets stay the source's.","summary":"A fork copies no assets, so a forked page's /_blob/<asset ID> URLs stay the source's and break when the source or that asset is deleted","tags":["forks","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/github.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.994958Z","id":"7bb059c47702678d9680a7f63eaee6a9d513b387ba14aa9c0117b7ab8ca1920f","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/github.rs:313-348, record d40983d3.\n\ncheck_quota counts the person's live artifacts (MemberCaps::max_artifacts, MEMBER_MAX_ARTIFACTS / [hosted] member_max_artifacts, default 200) and is called from create_artifact_async (crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs) and fork_artifact_async (crates/clax-core/src/store/forks.rs). Nothing bounds the bytes a member writes: new versions of their own artifacts, asset uploads and pushed commits are uncounted, so one member can fill the content store within MAX_ASSET_BYTES per upload and the version size limits. A byte cap needs a running per-account counter charged in the version and asset transactions (record_version_locked, upload_asset).","kind":"concern","ref":"git:dafbbbfb0e440885b354402b74705978ad070d7e","span":{"start":{"line":312},"end":{"line":347},"content_hash":"15906e486096e7696147bd11eeffb664687bc6851388db8b5581955b31076521"},"summary":"A GitHub member's account is capped by artifact count alone: no cap on stored bytes","tags":["deferred","hosted","github","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/github.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.994992Z","id":"b79ada9c7343bf9f5b33c9938212a509963ec4ac7c37f6ada1d39019076965c0","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/github.rs:356-362, record 77469ed5.\n\nblock_in sets github_identities.blocked_at when the owner revokes the person (Store::revoke_person in crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs), and github_sign_in refuses an account whose row is blocked or whose person is revoked. Nothing clears blocked_at, and People offers no unblock: the owner would have to edit the database to let the account back in.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:dafbbbfb0e440885b354402b74705978ad070d7e","span":{"start":{"line":355},"end":{"line":361},"content_hash":"486b8783435225a3efdbef07b2d4303c54f3f0933cfac0fe9f56f203b15132be"},"summary":"A blocked GitHub account cannot be unblocked","tags":["hosted","github","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.995242Z","id":"c7d64cc60b5c58a54fdddf71a734327f4b75e17c12f3178caf05aac74e9263d3","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/hosted.rs:297-333, record 245fe67c.\n\nThe prototype names a guest 'Name (guest)' wherever Clax shows a name to an agent or an approver. Here a guest is a plain viewer row with viewers.guest = 1; feedback, comments_read and approval views show the bare name. Names cannot collide with members' or other guests' (check_guest_name), which limits impersonation.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:4728cf5c20cb059a7675fcf56d04b297532ab930","span":{"start":{"line":297},"end":{"line":333},"content_hash":"fa6b1bcabd7d4ab1064bfd5c639d34232f3e0b5b95de9eb1b91c01616fba37b0"},"suggested_fix":"Mark guest authors in the agent-facing views and approval cards.","summary":"Guests are not labelled as guests to agents or approvers","tags":["hosted","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.995296Z","id":"d180d1282705f126ad829cbf70930679cb88b286da7649d253acf7ccaa496a7a","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/hosted.rs:858-862, record 3ac434ed.\n\nAn agent token is a bearer grant (grants.bearer = 1, its cxa_ token in grant_tokens, kept out of credential_index so it never passes the signed Clax-Grant path). The endpoint resolves Authorization: Bearer cxa_... with bearer_grant, then Store::grant_caller for its person and rights, and builds Caller::PersonAgent; no route accepts the token yet.","kind":"comment","ref":"git:4728cf5c20cb059a7675fcf56d04b297532ab930","span":{"start":{"line":858},"end":{"line":862},"content_hash":"6118ad026448bf7342835eef06f09082a183699f7c1c18391bc4c90fa653e306"},"summary":"Store::bearer_grant is how the remote MCP endpoint should authenticate an agent token","tags":["hosted","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.995628Z","id":"7750ff25b3fa63ac933a3aafa1fa150a53245a4ef53590578e5e700d94faa63a","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/inbox.rs:1405-1410, record 059505cb.\n\nconnection_decided reads a connection item only when the owner approves or denies the request (crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs approve_grant, deny_grant). A pending request that expires after 10 minutes (request_grant's stale sweep, expire_grants) leaves its item unread in the owner's inbox; once the unapproved row is purged a day later the item renders gone with connection null. Reading it at the lapse, or touching it so the shell shows the expired status, would need the lapse paths to call into the inbox.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":1405},"end":{"line":1410},"content_hash":"37faa7c25489c7bb21c58449a00b215ba4670c56c30156fd84acd0324fb5acb1"},"summary":"A connection request that lapses unanswered keeps its connection item unread","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.995748Z","id":"032c86b340159d69499c95f80fb7d5f52f7e969686bf9d72ff009bf0fe0e73be","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/inbox.rs:1637-1641, record cfb08a05.\n\nnote_finished makes the finished item for the session's person. A first publish by a person's agent reaches both the person and the owner (note_version), since a new artifact appears in the owner's gallery; finished work was left to the person, per spec §18 ('Inbox, questions: own').","kind":"alternative","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":1637},"end":{"line":1641},"content_hash":"a0fa4a8c2b1a39edfb532ddd9c70fe377bd2d0458f5500bbff31400339dff010"},"summary":"A connected person's agent's finished work reaches its person only, not the owner","tags":["revisit:the owner asks to follow other people's agents' work in their inbox","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.996038Z","id":"c08432b6d7d5662f38a5655c32779b5073f8137565c7a03ed9c7ff619658865e","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/linked.rs:378-382, record 064e84c8.\n\nremote_versions is written by pushes from migration 33 on. For an artifact pushed before, only the link's pushed_n/remote_n pair is known, so a public thread on an older public version is placed on the newest pushed local version and shown as 'on <remote> v<n>' though a twin exists.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:4203e8ad965dccfeb22f40ca44aeb3d1ba473f05","span":{"start":{"line":378},"end":{"line":382},"content_hash":"9a418a8e6498501aaef54bc63beafb59ae3045a16669f5a7f718a92c47fb405b"},"suggested_fix":"Backfill remote_versions on the next push by pairing the public copy's versions with the local ones in order when the link was never moved (no fork, no new).","summary":"Versions pushed before linked threads have no recorded twin but the link's last push","tags":["review","status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.996115Z","id":"3424593ce090c1763db0f5cfe8e13d2e5842f1a8f032f949d04a2dd5fea037ec","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/linked.rs:497-508, record 27a175c4.\n\nSync::mirror looks a remote thread up by (remote, remote thread ID) alone, so a remote that lists, under one public artifact, a thread ID belonging to another artifact linked to it writes into that other artifact's local thread. Only artifacts linked to that remote are reachable, and the remote can write to them anyway, so this is consistency rather than access.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:4203e8ad965dccfeb22f40ca44aeb3d1ba473f05","span":{"start":{"line":497},"end":{"line":508},"content_hash":"5d646f16c65cb93420f8638cd10f761cdf837fa7a9cf4122734478ccc796ece1"},"suggested_fix":"Also match remote_artifact_id (or artifact_id) of the link being read.","summary":"linked_thread_by_remote is not scoped to the link's artifact","tags":["review","linked-threads","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.996179Z","id":"b1ee4c55439f74899e1610fff38b6671fb8e6ad0d7996b4f61e0dfad52325ca2","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/linked.rs:632-665, record 51707e9f.\n\nSpec 2026-10-15-linked-threads-design (Authors) says a mirrored comment is stored with author kind remote. comments.author_kind carries CHECK (author_kind IN ('viewer','agent')) from migration 3, and feedback rows reference comments, so adding a kind needs a table rebuild under foreign keys. The comment is written as a viewer comment with no local public ID (or an agent comment of no session) and its remote kind, public ID and name are kept in linked_comments; views add linked.origin remote and agents read the author as '<name> (on <remote>)'. The author is never a local person either way.","kind":"alternative","ref":"git:4203e8ad965dccfeb22f40ca44aeb3d1ba473f05","span":{"start":{"line":632},"end":{"line":665},"content_hash":"1d315f12504beb532832435e36692c31c1b338debf63539814fd73b5727f1649"},"summary":"Mirrored comments keep a local author_kind viewer or agent, with the remote author in linked_comments, instead of author_kind remote","tags":["design","revisit:the comments table is next rebuilt","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.996241Z","id":"79630cf9e6f4ccc2c7a1f07c52924991890033684ba8eb9ef30a02b77e70835e","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/linked.rs:838-850, record 0d4172d0.\n\nthreads records no reopener, so scan_linked queues every reopen of a linked thread, while resolves go up only when the owner or an owner's agent resolved (resolved_by, resolved_by_person). Another local person who can see a linked thread and reopens it is reported there as the owner's person.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:4203e8ad965dccfeb22f40ca44aeb3d1ba473f05","span":{"start":{"line":838},"end":{"line":850},"content_hash":"68b1d810d48a25f82d340e55584a56333546f845fa14c5ade1f6e019b04812b5"},"suggested_fix":"Record who reopened a thread (reopened_by) and queue a reopen only when it is the owner's or an owner's agent's.","summary":"A reopen goes up as the token's person whoever reopened it here","tags":["review","security","status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.996544Z","id":"8896a2cf07b5bbd0e3b1713ef45ceddf626f5e8ab043506605d8914c91f2bb6b","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs:739-742, record eaa57b0c.\n\nFailure: a home at migration 25 where a person's agent asked a question (a dev home run on this branch) keeps that question's item with recipient NULL after 26, so it sits in the owner's inbox and crates/clax-server/src/inbox.rs render reads its question unscoped (st.question), showing the person's question and answers to the owner, while the person never gets the item. Main's homes hold no person sessions, so they are unaffected. Accepted: migrations 24-26 are unmerged (spec M27), so only a dev home run on this branch can hold such items; questions themselves get their person from their session (questions.person is filled in by the migration).","kind":"waiver","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":739},"end":{"line":742},"content_hash":"4611fbab17797ab78415d9f71e991c5b174e8ca88f75ff87d6685c7d8474fc79"},"summary":"Migration 26 leaves every existing inbox item the owner's, including question and finished items a connected person's agent made at schema 24-25","tags":["review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.996624Z","id":"72e1a0365764ae1e5a641c5e52cc6734f04321d03e99b65273ac386056386d18","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs:774-776, record fa9ef7ec.","kind":"comment","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":774},"end":{"line":776},"content_hash":"7b8c2cfc4b3987a8e331333cde1cdfbfbebd527f736765bcd9ae5f2176add692"},"summary":"Migration 27 (hosted sign-in) takes the next number after multi-person's 26; it renumbers if another branch lands first","tags":["hosted","merge","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.996704Z","id":"e022ca731a8267befdbee499dfd70bf80fca250edd71536ae7789165d3ccd53b","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs:808-930, record 44826f12.","kind":"comment","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":808},"end":{"line":930},"content_hash":"4fc246c7ef2dbffa199d9a8cf44a6b8c266dcff13243c43bab8ce3914f210925"},"summary":"Migration 30 (publishing to a public Clax) follows akesling/clax-artifacts' 29 (sessions.client_name); it renumbers if another branch lands a 30 first. It also rebuilds inbox_items to add the `push` kind, as migration 26 left the table.","tags":["migrations","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.996772Z","id":"b8105a392f24efa6bc643ed0bec3bbd2a0ab77196f5d161eb04c89c5000aba45","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs:888-895, record 924ede60.\n\nSmall rows, but they outlive the artifact and the grant. Dropping keys of revoked grants or older than some months would bound it.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":888},"end":{"line":895},"content_hash":"3809d3eb40206bf1050d7706a17caa1d82c06599c44bd8c816fb14753e919899"},"summary":"publish_keys is never pruned: one row per version an agent token published with a key","tags":["deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.996842Z","id":"968d74e24c937a53279bd1935eb9518998cb23c40fe012e53b6d61e55b174d65","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs:931-948, record 388db751.","kind":"comment","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":931},"end":{"line":948},"content_hash":"7d8c751bbf9693818ae00c620d322851f29dceeee90a9880b0582ce408b23081"},"summary":"Migration 31 (GitHub identities) follows akesling/clax-artifacts' 30 (publishing to a public Clax); it renumbers if another branch lands a 31 first","tags":["migrations","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.996909Z","id":"04e01c765df218cd9c8312c9cbb882c2615e1d9fe6a1b734e34a1ac96bf7e7bc","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs:1001-1014, record bb077166.\n\nthread_id is the PRIMARY KEY; scan_linked queues a fresh local thread only when no linked_threads row names it (crates/clax-core/src/store/linked.rs scan_linked), so the first remote scanned takes it and the other never gets it, nor its replies. Threads mirrored from either remote are separate local threads.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":1001},"end":{"line":1014},"content_hash":"422e16fad9ac387965892c1a684d9f7f45d108c71b2cd3fbe0fa9890e34ef65e"},"summary":"linked_threads is keyed by the local thread alone, so an artifact linked to two remotes sends its local threads to only one of them","tags":["review","linked-threads","revisit:an artifact is pushed to a second remote","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.996971Z","id":"a58bd84e0d2804e7ec40da9b07e779d8e4df15c451cad189c2208f9f9b1298ff","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs:1052-1059, record 7dd62168.\n\nA hosted daemon keeps every key a linked local daemon's up-sends named (crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs comment_key), as publish_keys keeps every publish's. Rows are small, but nothing removes them, not even when the thread or grant is deleted.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":1052},"end":{"line":1059},"content_hash":"4ba09b7472a4ca6e5001974915649601eee612783ece3677d8a9dc4398698508"},"suggested_fix":"Delete a grant's keys with the grant and a thread's with the thread, or prune keys older than the outbox could resend (a day).","summary":"comment_keys is never pruned: one row per thread or comment an agent token wrote with an Idempotency-Key","tags":["review","status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.997031Z","id":"00c5000167bdb7f982510f61c39a508ec8c07fc9eb9a6e84b4771a0aa533e3ac","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs:1095-1101, record e614fbdc.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":1095},"end":{"line":1101},"content_hash":"40e0ef842deae344eeb6cb9ab562cb44f1e01fd90bba9720a79e05d2a441f941"},"summary":"question_keys is never pruned: one row per question an agent token asked with an Idempotency-Key","tags":["linked-threads","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.997309Z","id":"fb83a7fe7afcd453363b4e3fdfa4b0d1ca2b6a3eb8d48bce7df5277bfe4d7ac5","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/mod.rs:757-783, record 102e3b6a.\n\nMeasured on this machine (load average about 45): the clax-core lib tests take 12.4 s with --skip the_store_tests_pass_on_one_connection and 20.8 s with it, since the child runs 455 tests after the parent's. The threshold `passed > 300` passes with 455; a module dropped from the filter (or from test_util::store) loses its coverage on one connection without failing it.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":767},"end":{"line":793},"content_hash":"b3bfd31319c95da4542d5ac7bd7f9fa165b3082f4e9534f5f055a9a24bdcbbee"},"suggested_fix":"Compare `passed` against the count the same filter lists (`--list`) less the ignored ones, or pin the module set.","summary":"The one-connection rerun adds about 8 s to the clax-core unit suite, and its >300 threshold only catches an empty filter","tags":["wasm","gate-speed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.997690Z","id":"6ccf71040fe24e020493791b11873af854da1fb8d8fa1eac28a30f95b6707bc9","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs:1129-1143, record 04ea4881.\n\nFor flow invite the grant's events carry grant_id and person but not invite_id, so the journal cannot join invite.create to the grant made from it except by person and time; invites.grant_id holds the link only while the row lives.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":1129},"end":{"line":1143},"content_hash":"a055d17fb6d13921d9565129c8f0b702f534ab8d657151596b97465c24004831"},"suggested_fix":"Add invite_id to grant.request (flow invite) and to audit spec section 6.13 and multi-person spec section 20.2.","summary":"An invite-flow grant.request and grant.approve do not name the invite they redeemed","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.997825Z","id":"f9a6a1dbe9922a1c6feb2e722e6af9a574735869f028ff4eb6512e4305680416","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs:1518-1610, record b5061b84.\n\napprove_owner_on_connect is the single approval made without a browser (spec section 21 item 3, M15). It is bounded to the connect: once per grant, within OWNER_ANSWER_SECS (10 minutes) of the tokens' issue, never once the person has made or revoked any approval of the owner (409 owner_answered, so a revocation in People stands; 409 answer_closed after the window), replays refused by accept_t first. Only the continuation token says it, never the access token agents sign with (crates/clax-server/tests/api_grants.rs a_connected_machine_approves_the_owner_through_its_continuation), and clax connect refuses on an agent channel (crates/clax-cli/tests/connect.rs connect_refuses_on_an_agent_channel). What remains: a process of the person's that reads remote.json within those ten minutes, before clax connect answers, could answer yes for them; the person can revoke it in People, and that revocation is final. Tests: store::people::tests::connecting_records_the_persons_approval_of_the_owner_once, the_answer_about_the_owner_never_overrides_the_person.","kind":"waiver","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":1518},"end":{"line":1610},"content_hash":"bc869590daace3db7ebb285095a3671207be9e1c25756a2f7a794eecb61f7838"},"summary":"The person's approval of the owner is recorded without a browser once, at connect: an agent present then could answer for the person","tags":["security","spec:6.3","spec:21","M15","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/pushes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.998030Z","id":"21408fbc3461f529c576398df20037d37e37302cd720d40e4993a919f8b29fc3","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/pushes.rs:144-152, record d3d39306.\n\nA refused commit stays on main (it is neither recorded nor tagged), and the stand-in refuses non-fast-forward pushes (clax-git ServeOptions deny_non_fast_forwards), so the only way past it is a push over it by someone who may publish. That commit is recorded with every file changed since the newest version authored by its pusher (record_push), so a refused or revoked person's changes reach other people's agents as, say, the owner's under the visibility filter; its note names the refused commits. The hosted prototype credits a changed blob to every author it already had in history (hosted/src/do/artifact.ts recordPushes, blobAuthors); here a refused commit's blobs have no recorded author. Fix: credit paths whose blob equals one in a refused commit to that commit's pusher as well, or refuse the commit over it until those paths match the newest version.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:ceb68d89ddb1093063205296d2bc440d12630f5a","span":{"start":{"line":145},"end":{"line":153},"content_hash":"8c34d7356614154fc05784b37020214d4aab0dc8a7a3271396030174350c9b1e"},"summary":"A commit recorded over refused commits carries their changes as its own pusher's words","tags":["security","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/pushes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.998069Z","id":"f3f7661c5d334f6586ee72deeba5ba75b02ba0e8319faa6dfcb469e017472491","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/pushes.rs:475-487, record 6d8f2fc3.\n\nPushes to Artifacts' own git endpoint never pass RepoDO, so RepoDO's ledger has no git_pushes row for their commits (crates/clax-worker/src/repos/db.rs record_push, written only by tokens::note_push from RepoDO's /git/ route), and the queue consumer reconciles with Pusher::default() (crates/clax-worker/src/lib.rs queue). pushers_of then gives every such commit the fallback, the owner: the owner becomes the version's publisher and the author of its changed files, and Store::standing allows it, whoever held the Artifacts token. clax_git::events::event_repo reads only the repository's name; the event's documented payload (ref, before, after, commits; crates/clax-git/src/events.rs:21-25) names no token or actor that is known here. Fix: once the pushed event's schema names the token (Artifacts tokens are entered in git_tokens with hash NULL by tokens::mint) or the actor, have the queue consumer enter a git_pushes row for the event's after commit with that token's holder before it asks the instance to reconcile.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:ceb68d89ddb1093063205296d2bc440d12630f5a","span":{"start":{"line":476},"end":{"line":488},"content_hash":"38cc39ea7d33382de52e273c944e0c51a787210b5289531ea9b52b303e7a18bd"},"summary":"A push straight to Cloudflare Artifacts is credited to the owner and passes the rights recheck as the owner","tags":["security","revisit:Cloudflare Artifacts' pushed-event schema is known","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.998275Z","id":"969acbf2d44509cec80c9172c293f1150199696737969269a6403045c233ee86","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/remotes.rs:323-335, record 809ea47e.\n\nIt is an outbound credential the daemon presents to the public Clax on every push, so it cannot be hashed like the inbound tokens the store verifies. It never appears in a view (Remote has no token field; tests/api_remotes.rs checks no listing carries cxa_), an event or an audit record. When a sign-in connects, the daemon makes the home 0700 and the database's files 0600 (crates/clax-server/src/routes/remotes.rs owner_only; checked in api_remotes's connect). A home copied elsewhere carries it: clax remote remove revokes it there, or the public People page does. Moving it to the OS keychain would protect a copied home but needs code the Durable Object build must not compile.","kind":"waiver","ref":"git:69750b2990275429f946bb32d6d188b3e9d50145","span":{"start":{"line":323},"end":{"line":335},"content_hash":"fd9f0bd8892117130346d36e0afcd15890f15c5a754e582aba89c15a40ae038f"},"summary":"A remote's agent token is kept as it is in the home's database (remotes.token), not hashed","tags":["security","revisit:a home is synced or backed up off the machine","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/sessions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.998656Z","id":"09207249f22a63c797ed1c513e566cf15b9176e37766466dbcb56f10e86ea6d2","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs:214-220, record 2c203ab3.\n\nRegistration derives a name from the repository and branch (spec section 11) without an event; session.start's body is harness, harness_session_id, cwd, transcript_path and pid. The first agent.name then reports previous: <derived name> with no earlier event naming it, and an @name in a comment cannot be tied to its session from the journal alone.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":189},"end":{"line":195},"content_hash":"2531645c1bbef5581474f3318cd70a2a599ab739af3be8223fbe8da994159a5b"},"suggested_fix":"Add name (classed as a name for redaction) to session.start and session.join bodies, and say so in audit spec section 6.8.","summary":"A session's derived name is never recorded, so agent.name's previous names a value the journal never held","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/sessions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.998781Z","id":"2961ece31c461480f8a74711bd5cbf8072cf11c40694992bb70bed1e454e4d9f","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs:1319-1348, record 2f7ad0c3.\n\nroutes/sessions.rs register calls end_bearer_sessions_beyond(gid, BEARER_SESSION_CAP - 1) and then register_session_restoring in separate transactions; concurrent initializes of one token can each count the same live set. The next registration trims it back. Accepted as a bound on build-up, not an exact limit.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":1296},"end":{"line":1325},"content_hash":"8ef33f44d4f1cafe046fb180228494b8e47afb2f14aca6b7df5ba45bf9f7a4bc"},"summary":"Two agent-token registrations at once can each leave room for themselves, so a token briefly holds more than BEARER_SESSION_CAP live sessions","tags":["hosted","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/sessions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.998882Z","id":"602f988bb3d7e0165e6026e3b635dfbd820ba01dde042f139a6b4c36ad3d742c","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs:1730-1746, record 8d99d26f.\n\nrelease_owned_in (crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs) selects threads WHERE target_session_id = ?1, and Store::roster groups threads by target_session_id; crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs indexes neither. Both are full scans of threads: off the request hot paths (ends, the reaper, GET /api/agents) and cheap at today's sizes, but linear in all threads ever made.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":1709},"end":{"line":1725},"content_hash":"ed1cb058eed0b38a9d4e07ae6c733539b4ca4c1c6388d6f7a4614ccf4b5c1af2"},"suggested_fix":"Add CREATE INDEX threads_by_target ON threads(target_session_id) WHERE target_session_id IS NOT NULL in the next migration.","summary":"Every session end and every roster read scans threads for target_session_id, which has no index","tags":["perf","revisit:the next migration on this branch","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/shares.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.999096Z","id":"3b63b900cef39fb78cbbbd827efcab83dfc14527172cd3b3bc2a6e3b8bbd7e66","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/shares.rs:331-346, record 87ab348f.\n\nshare_artifact resolves a login through github_identities.login, which is refreshed only at each sign-in (crates/clax-core/src/store/github.rs link). If account A signed in as 'octo', later renamed on GitHub and never signed in here again, and someone else now holds 'octo' on GitHub, a share to '@octo' binds to A's person, not to whoever owns the login today. A login no one here has signed in with waits and binds at its first sign-in, which is safe: from then on the share follows the person, not the login (tested in shares.rs a_login_share_waits_for_its_first_sign_in_then_follows_the_person).","kind":"concern","ref":"git:dafbbbfb0e440885b354402b74705978ad070d7e","span":{"start":{"line":331},"end":{"line":346},"content_hash":"0f48399d24676bee458098b796956398d96ef690dc90960df446288dc6c15847"},"suggested_fix":"Look the login up on GitHub's API (GET /users/<login>) when sharing, and bind by numeric ID.","summary":"A share by GitHub login binds at once to whichever account last signed in with that login here, which may be stale after a rename","tags":["security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/shares.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.999148Z","id":"3561332cb0a396d0c3108f501b9b050c474a1f7079f2ca9063ec3cd9c77ae3a2","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/shares.rs:333-346, record 95291e43.\n\nshare_artifact's login lookup (github_identities joined to viewers) checks only that the row is not the owner's; it does not read github_identities.blocked_at or viewers.person_revoked_at. ShareTo::Person refuses a revoked person (unknown_person), so the two paths disagree. No access follows (a blocked account cannot sign in and a revoked person's grants end), but the sharer sees the share as granted to a named person rather than refused.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:dafbbbfb0e440885b354402b74705978ad070d7e","span":{"start":{"line":333},"end":{"line":346},"content_hash":"32639782b0a4356b493eedf2bea40b3ee1b0c257d7eecf9ed56009cab56ffc0f"},"suggested_fix":"Refuse such a login as ShareTo::Person refuses a revoked person, or show the share as blocked.","summary":"A share by login binds to an account whose GitHub identity is blocked or whose person is revoked, and the dialog lists it as an ordinary person","tags":["sharing","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.999444Z","id":"115c3cbdc86d98ea5bc94a48ad2a2f52ab71f94f5c089139932e60823be5b9a7","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/threads.rs:841-853, record f05ee8bd.\n\nBefore 274f3832 the clip was written inside the thread transaction after the liveness, version and anchor checks. create_thread_inner now takes the content lock, checks liveness and puts the clip first; invalid_anchor, unknown_version and route checks fail later in the transaction and the clip is removed at threads.rs:926. A failed removal is only logged, leaving an unreferenced clip under clips/ (FsContent) or the clip-<thread> asset key. The content lock also makes a clipped thread wait for a publish of the same artifact in progress. Checking the version and anchor in a read before the put would keep refusals free of content I/O.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":840},"end":{"line":852},"content_hash":"da9c324b36bc56145b156ff2a9e326de501b4210777bf1a14697ddd9bfe8b870"},"summary":"A clipped thread now writes its clip before the version and anchor are checked, so every refused clipped request writes and deletes a clip","tags":["content-store","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/viewers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.999680Z","id":"1b9f7857c6dfd58cb122b41f4ba1acc1b7e3b1eb355fc1782a1f0e7e44592269","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/viewers.rs:122-144, record 8d5ba8ae.\n\nAt 8446429: upsert_viewer(lan, 'Аlex') with no owner name succeeds; set_owner_name('Alex') then succeeds too, and both names stand. An agent registering from repository web is named 'web' beside a LAN viewer 'wеb'. New people are covered (check_person_name refuses a look-alike held by an uninvited viewer). The owner usually names themselves late, on a first comment, so pre-squatting is the likely order.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":122},"end":{"line":144},"content_hash":"f1c9ce822f6f3ec3cbd80cb2a8bf008c8cf80b2dadb35ac47a7f759a60d0a91f"},"suggested_fix":"Mark it where names are shown: an unconnected viewer whose name looks like a protected name is flagged in the shell and in agent author lines (with spec section 9.6's '(not connected)', Task 17), rather than refusing the owner their own name.","summary":"The look-alike check runs only when the later name is set: a LAN viewer who took 'Аlex' before the owner named themselves 'Alex', or 'wеb' before an agent web went live, keeps it","tags":["review","spec:9.6","revisit:task-17","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.845366Z","id":"b781046632a9b1b98188ae6a8eb45970878c61a3f2beceb75b84ff276c702e32","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs:1112-1121, record 1e165437.\n\nSpec §9.3: 'Declining keeps the rows held; a later ask there makes a new request only after 10 minutes'. request_in applies the same quiet period to routing, so a sender pressing Send again right after the approver declined does not re-announce the request; the rows are held and the agent's placeholder reads as not asked. If the owner wants a deliberate re-send to ask at once, drop the check for Cause::Routing.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:3cadd457","span":{"start":{"line":1126},"end":{"line":1135},"content_hash":"cf9707d61e55687d29484ea3ec1da7a8faa513bbca583c591bf81438ce7a4e23"},"summary":"A routed send within ten minutes of a decline makes no request, though spec §9.3 names only ask","supersedes":"4616e47c7730423a92ba80cfdb72d0a378d7f88c795bc7dffe8eef7e210b4b97","tags":["people","spec:9.3","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.864413Z","id":"88673a6f317a460d8566fe6f64750fe9ff6671a3dbaa29b1e916ec60417bd59b","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs:1286-1306, record 9f25f03b.\n\nwithheld_in_thread counts the authors withheld from each comment body (the rows a take holds, spec M16). A thread whose comments the agent may see but whose anchor, clip or artifact title is another person's (spec §3.3 step 6) is delivered with those fields placeholdered and makes no request; the agent can ask for the artifact's content outside threads with ask {approval: {url_or_id}} (Store::ask_approval, withheld_outside_threads), which covers text fields, the current version, documents and assets, but not a thread's anchor.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:3cadd457","span":{"start":{"line":1300},"end":{"line":1320},"content_hash":"2db7bc0ea49daabf8d49defd3d54488b8041d0c22a95068bc6531cfc23d68cee"},"summary":"Routing asks only for the authors of comment bodies; a withheld anchor, clip, batch note or title makes no request","supersedes":"897cdd91477c74122263714ef2c09ba64db264aead09f8a3f284c3108184f372","tags":["people","spec:9.2","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.883448Z","id":"b8689b374b17e063ecc28b1fe7ba12da41727e469900b7cdc94c439b69062efd","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs:1898-1908, record bfa6b632.\n\nThe overflow marker (install row approval_overflow:<approver>) lists the [author, artifact, thread] places whose routed content request_in held without a request, past MAX_OPEN_REQUESTS (100) per approver or MAX_OPEN_PER_AUTHOR (20) per author. Only Store::decide_request rechecks them, dropping a place once its content is no longer held without a request (held_without_request: answered by an open or declined request, delivered, gone, or now visible). A withdrawal or an approval made outside a decision changes nothing until the next decision, so the banner can outlive what it counted.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:3cadd457","span":{"start":{"line":1912},"end":{"line":1922},"content_hash":"e605efbaa1b77ac65394cb92bbe3b8380e6925c8a3c4e43692703b6852ef04e5"},"summary":"People's overflow banner stays up after withdrawals bring an approver under the limit, until their next decision","supersedes":"4e99c5ba140ed3ad4f2089b684fe49bc976fbac2289c291158be039169f4c186","tags":["people","spec:9.2","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/exec.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.902357Z","id":"6994f9b1b4eb6a225409e1ec9fc54143052bcc85d38216601b4796ba446773cb","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/exec.rs:66-89, record c1fa8f66.\n\nSeen in Linux perf runs: a single commit held up by the disk. The writer runs WAL with SQLite's default synchronous=FULL, so every commit syncs the WAL, and the background PASSIVE checkpoint runs every CHECKPOINT_INTERVAL (2 s). Every delivery of a write waits on its commit, so one slow commit moves a whole cluster of deliveries (scripts/perf-clients.py:23-29 explains how the realtime gate copes).","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":246},"end":{"line":269},"content_hash":"19a1b1cc49fe118705a9d82f6b9227495d66a06ae11378ed14f24dfb809e7ed5"},"suggested_fix":"Measure commit times on Linux with synchronous=NORMAL (durable across a crash of the process, not of the machine, in WAL mode) and with a different checkpoint cadence before choosing.","summary":"On Linux, store commits occasionally take 25 to 120 ms","supersedes":"a1abac78188a15fada17e8991dd6ffd8caa0a07b79a872f0dcc758d68deac4bb","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.921553Z","id":"0db014c35d02c074f97d8859e1e1140b487901bc594c7f80b96dbc53a9c3c846","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs:2116-2123, record 4efdda9a.\n\nDelivery::changed_for tells a person of a change only when their rows' newest time (StateRow::stamp: created, delivered, acknowledged, told, untargeted, last sent, session end) is the thread's newest. A change that sets no time (a watch armed or disarmed, which changes a sent row's waiting tier; a codex queue failure; a handoff that keeps a row's times) is published to the owner but to no person, so a connected person's open card keeps the old tier until the thread is fetched again. The owner hears every change.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:3cadd457","span":{"start":{"line":2130},"end":{"line":2137},"content_hash":"ae60d870fe573bb59b841ba7c4a344861a791c29f05330219c9330e9d6ad8e3e"},"summary":"A change that stamps no row reaches only the owner live; a person sees it at their next fetch","supersedes":"ff9f942a8c9b632eb661afb4b27fd0b47f8b567b53e3e114d974be830f7c16b9","tags":["people","spec:10","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.942975Z","id":"9b4671a3fa070a0d299e4dbe94b60c480d562a2e234fc6dd55f8cb7a299a3888","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs:2160-2169, record ddeebf95.\n\nstate_of reports withheld (the target session's person as approver) from placeholder_at, which a take sets when it holds and tells a row, or while an open approval request of that person covers the row's comment author there (a send naming the agent, spec §10). A comment that joins no request (a send naming no agent, a later reply whose author has no open request there, an author held past the request limits) reads sent, waiting on its tier, until the agent's next take. Computing it from visibility at state time would build a Visibility per target session's person inside feedback_states_in, which listings call for every thread (spec §8.7 cost).","kind":"concern","ref":"git:3cadd457","span":{"start":{"line":2174},"end":{"line":2183},"content_hash":"00e0bbcb6caac54ad3191169bbd4afe7db0534f84731d8080a14ad9755c4d0d0"},"summary":"A held row that no open request covers reads sent until a take holds it","supersedes":"13d79c95856a48d0f4b710db96131c6ca4fe3f99af74dca5dd3c6760b127dcc1","tags":["people","spec:8.4","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.965876Z","id":"314e74125566ec5319b77e5147b3d9c691e9447f003f345a0aee05b1a3640100","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/inbox.rs:1363-1368, record 0118687f.\n\nconnection_decided reads a connection item only when the owner approves or denies the request (crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs approve_grant, deny_grant). A pending request that expires after 10 minutes (request_grant's stale sweep, expire_grants) leaves its item unread in the owner's inbox; once the unapproved row is purged a day later the item renders gone with connection null. Reading it at the lapse, or touching it so the shell shows the expired status, would need the lapse paths to call into the inbox.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":1388},"end":{"line":1393},"content_hash":"c1c86e26871ba066020c75f1d9b1b954ee91add027a8fb30f98694a07930d59d"},"summary":"A connection request that lapses unanswered keeps its connection item unread","supersedes":"9facff47b5fff8e74f47ea46f477bfb141db7978ee7435f1056cbc8334f089e0","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.987789Z","id":"c4826cf52130d479a045154c976c46d2696e038062c532f03e396310f92b7e10","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/inbox.rs:1552-1556, record 6014047e.\n\nnote_finished makes the finished item for the session's person. A first publish by a person's agent reaches both the person and the owner (note_version), since a new artifact appears in the owner's gallery; finished work was left to the person, per spec §18 ('Inbox, questions: own').","kind":"alternative","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":1592},"end":{"line":1596},"content_hash":"df46c2781c4e06aa0fe53e6fadd564b9bcbcad9e060403b47de165ac7d60413a"},"summary":"A connected person's agent's finished work reaches its person only, not the owner","supersedes":"d9ae8606a1af43bd153efdc4cdfbd410db028cdbd8c65eca4a519b1d26dda71b","tags":["revisit:the owner asks to follow other people's agents' work in their inbox","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:35.010245Z","id":"e9d6932d46817207d8a8fa6cfeb59d04be600176af7791c240b87cfb702dba27","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs:1088-1102, record b5059e16.\n\nFor flow invite the grant's events carry grant_id and person but not invite_id, so the journal cannot join invite.create to the grant made from it except by person and time; invites.grant_id holds the link only while the row lives.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":1117},"end":{"line":1131},"content_hash":"5797052e7ab6d41d1c7e1138621f9475ea1bbb4d84154b5bc865aea2b46b476f"},"suggested_fix":"Add invite_id to grant.request (flow invite) and to audit spec section 6.13 and multi-person spec section 20.2.","summary":"An invite-flow grant.request and grant.approve do not name the invite they redeemed","supersedes":"2c328526a81cda80fc952edde60d11804357d9dd5b920bee632c8eb27a4511b1","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:35.032294Z","id":"9de6ef359975cc995a7761da3ad0c8c793bce195708af226f90df5562b0a17ec","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs:1477-1569, record fbaca2aa.\n\napprove_owner_on_connect is the single approval made without a browser (spec section 21 item 3, M15). It is bounded to the connect: once per grant, within OWNER_ANSWER_SECS (10 minutes) of the tokens' issue, never once the person has made or revoked any approval of the owner (409 owner_answered, so a revocation in People stands; 409 answer_closed after the window), replays refused by accept_t first. Only the continuation token says it, never the access token agents sign with (crates/clax-server/tests/api_grants.rs a_connected_machine_approves_the_owner_through_its_continuation), and clax connect refuses on an agent channel (crates/clax-cli/tests/connect.rs connect_refuses_on_an_agent_channel). What remains: a process of the person's that reads remote.json within those ten minutes, before clax connect answers, could answer yes for them; the person can revoke it in People, and that revocation is final. Tests: store::people::tests::connecting_records_the_persons_approval_of_the_owner_once, the_answer_about_the_owner_never_overrides_the_person.","kind":"waiver","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":1506},"end":{"line":1598},"content_hash":"5d260869dffa70dec7dfc40d7ad1104c236566f218f6537d20ff488531c27bd3"},"summary":"The person's approval of the owner is recorded without a browser once, at connect: an agent present then could answer for the person","supersedes":"5978aff9195dfb72a0d2532585acb7cfc49d84441f5befde8c01c885863a633f","tags":["security","spec:6.3","spec:21","M15","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/sessions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:35.065677Z","id":"a3de722a5081600f0a8cd360dabcab4775aae88ea525df61a0bbf50e14ba5d8a","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs:213-219, record d9e10887.\n\nRegistration derives a name from the repository and branch (spec section 11) without an event; session.start's body is harness, harness_session_id, cwd, transcript_path and pid. The first agent.name then reports previous: <derived name> with no earlier event naming it, and an @name in a comment cannot be tied to its session from the journal alone.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":189},"end":{"line":195},"content_hash":"2531645c1bbef5581474f3318cd70a2a599ab739af3be8223fbe8da994159a5b"},"suggested_fix":"Add name (classed as a name for redaction) to session.start and session.join bodies, and say so in audit spec section 6.8.","summary":"A session's derived name is never recorded, so agent.name's previous names a value the journal never held","supersedes":"6146447fbc2c0620a01b1199ea38beec43fbf714e038bd0c6da07618a6f2da37","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/sessions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:35.095731Z","id":"347b05564c9c8cb862bd2ded4413588f966d8c47753ed42434a8833353a9b86d","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs:1639-1655, record bcb6cc4e.\n\nrelease_owned_in (crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs) selects threads WHERE target_session_id = ?1, and Store::roster groups threads by target_session_id; crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs indexes neither. Both are full scans of threads: off the request hot paths (ends, the reaper, GET /api/agents) and cheap at today's sizes, but linear in all threads ever made.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":1697},"end":{"line":1713},"content_hash":"20c6bc83236711f3d0fd91be27eb8807d928e32beb5474638e9b1e8ace251388"},"suggested_fix":"Add CREATE INDEX threads_by_target ON threads(target_session_id) WHERE target_session_id IS NOT NULL in the next migration.","summary":"Every session end and every roster read scans threads for target_session_id, which has no index","supersedes":"905a0b004c57352857dfd4b94cc1178fd740114a79f658ed9292fe17c4b0c7b5","tags":["perf","revisit:the next migration on this branch","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/viewers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:35.114944Z","id":"6b31d5488c4d6b6ed8a5996b14726dfa614390f2abae727a0fd31a3581bef4af","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/viewers.rs:210-227, record 93ccd2dd.\n\nMigration 24 hashes every existing viewer's row ID into viewer_cookies with legacy = 1 so existing LAN viewers keep their identity; a legacy cookie never names a person (VIEWER_BY_COOKIE), a viewer made a person loses its legacy cookies (create_invite), and GET /api/viewers/me replaces one with a cxv_ secret (reissue_viewer_cookie). Until that call, someone who minted viewers in the same millisecond as the victim on main could still act as that anonymous viewer (comment, rename): the pre-branch exposure, now bounded to unvisited anonymous viewers. Retiring every legacy cookie at once (say, at the first daemon start after a fixed date) would close it at the cost of those viewers' identities.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":214},"end":{"line":231},"content_hash":"8299dae6a186c40de75360a6569a05295050802db3e965a3637151f5d3dafa4f"},"summary":"An anonymous LAN viewer migrated from main keeps its guessable legacy cookie (its row ID, a monotonic ULID) until that browser next calls GET /api/viewers/me","supersedes":"bcc550ca536dc1431c1a6bcd1c499a6c025eee49e37da1cc520a7ff02c4534aa","tags":["final-review","security","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:42:16.613626Z","id":"f9280da32dc9d04a69743882aa2cf69ed28b3b7490cd633f9d1f13040232665f","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"6dbd24d8ca07de749b55acdb966d0f733668729ba077d8793a3208070c02dafe","summary":"The hosted/ files this record cites were removed in 60298c1d (the TypeScript prototype's retirement); read one at its parent with git show 60298c1d^:hosted/<path>","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:42:16.763216Z","id":"80843f5a3fc6f0a36a6b8df6a93c0f7dcbc962348373e51c1e3ad0c78752f53a","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"2bb2a20501aa96b3d24691a54b758269a798de3a5dddf58830ca8827f4bcde57","summary":"Since 274f3832 clip images live in the content store and the paths handed to agents come from ContentStore::local_clip and local_file (None, so null or a 'no file on this machine' snapshot line, for a store that keeps no files). Still on the home's files, as local tooling documented in the store module's Content section: backfill.rs's hashing of old homes, stray_version_dirs, stray_asset_temp_files (both find nothing where read_dir is Unsupported), AssetRow::path and clax doctor's version_files check. Whether that is the intended end state is the owner's call.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:42:16.782854Z","id":"33a854fd2606778e038efe219eafeec6b5a9cc3fb3f53c7dfb5c78507efe6b44","body":{"detail":"A watch armed or disarmed, a codex queue failure and a handoff that keeps times change only the tier text of a sent row ('waiting on the agent finishing its current work' and the like); every decision reaches its approver and author (publish_decision), so no person keeps a stale hold, decline or approval from these. Two gaps remain: (1) a comment a page wrote has several authors (page_authors), and a decision's parties name only the request's author, so the page's other authors read the row (Delivery::sees) but hear nothing of the decision until they fetch; code reading. (2) The hub's repeat suppression (crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs project, ch.delivery) remembers the last state sent per recipient key and channel, not what the client applied, so a reader whose client dropped a state (a new thread's state arriving before its thread event: record on crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs:539-573) or that fetched after an unsent change is not sent that state again.","kind":"comment","references":"4d2b858384a4a0293cc04b0b134dc2465286797341ec5a926cd75d215550866e","summary":"Assessment: the unstamped changes only move a waiting tier, which misleads no one; two cases do leave a person reading a wrong state","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:42:16.783040Z","id":"4807536ad708e0cbf20c6ff9d76263c0adafa6022a223437564f205d3c7872da","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"4d2b858384a4a0293cc04b0b134dc2465286797341ec5a926cd75d215550866e","summary":"Two gaps reply 65115b61 named are closed in c84e0d7a: a decision now reaches the content's co-authors (Delivery::decision_people), and the hub forgets what it sent a person when a stream of theirs subscribes or resumes. The tier staleness this record describes stays.","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/forks.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:42:16.821608Z","id":"710c5c38e788a5f11f6703327c1d523f00a6f0ac07b574a52798ccde858f14ad","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"7a64361dfb8f3d6d4d130bbdd95fdcae6f1b6ba7c5cb5bcb0ad93b55649cb8a4","summary":"The hosted/ files this record cites were removed in 60298c1d (the TypeScript prototype's retirement); read one at its parent with git show 60298c1d^:hosted/<path>","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:42:16.933655Z","id":"d5767efb9f29805ec2a22453a8145cceb6198d815dac954253bc00766ee8b4c0","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"7750ff25b3fa63ac933a3aafa1fa150a53245a4ef53590578e5e700d94faa63a","summary":"The owner can now mark such an item read from its card (ConnectionCard's Mark read, 2eb5ce4a); the lapse paths still leave it unread.","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:42:17.066379Z","id":"ac8f19d86e4f42ff8cb7215079e0fcd43bac2b9f25b6cfe2260dd3cc4bd39df9","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"72e1a0365764ae1e5a641c5e52cc6734f04321d03e99b65273ac386056386d18","summary":"Checked on 2026-10-13: every rust-* branch and multi-person end at 26, so 27 is the next free number on akesling/clax-artifacts; branch flutter-app (from main at 23) also writes a migration 27 (model use by apps) after its own 24 to 26, so whichever lands second renumbers.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/pushes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:42:17.257876Z","id":"56d635bd9dd120cec0727ee4a0af507d80f2fe801a37d784c71503dda38cbb43","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"21408fbc3461f529c576398df20037d37e37302cd720d40e4993a919f8b29fc3","summary":"The hosted/ files this record cites were removed in 60298c1d (the TypeScript prototype's retirement); read one at its parent with git show 60298c1d^:hosted/<path>","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/pushes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:42:17.276689Z","id":"1fe07f3978b3ab8094df4824ad1619340655c736597a9f76291c2cbe3a6d9b78","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"f3f7661c5d334f6586ee72deeba5ba75b02ba0e8319faa6dfcb469e017472491","summary":"Since 4f1f7191 no member or member's agent gets a write token where pushes are credited to the owner (crates/clax-server/src/git_remotes.rs credited, push_unattributed), so the tokens this instance mints reach this path only for the owner and the owner's agents. A token minted on the Cloudflare dashboard or by the Artifacts API directly still pushes as the owner.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/viewers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:42:17.428754Z","id":"735686c21e576ee150d5f55ed6cd6a3279fe8223560d5c3fd861fade89a24ca2","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"1b9f7857c6dfd58cb122b41f4ba1acc1b7e3b1eb355fc1782a1f0e7e44592269","summary":"The agent side of the suggested fix landed in 7e11f344 and 35cec880: every name of a viewer who is neither the owner nor a person reads '<name> (not connected)' in what an agent gets (feedback items and their author lines, batch senders, withheld authors, thread comments, resolved_by_name, artifact participants; crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs Connected::label, crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs mark_thread). A LAN viewer named 'Аlex' therefore reads 'Аlex (not connected)' to the owner's agents (api_people::unconnected_authors_are_marked_not_connected). The shell's flag for such a viewer is still open, for the People and thread-card UI.","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
