{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T16:19:13.450723Z","id":"d774bf8a61470a5710397d813a95e22f90179cb072f7ee0454134c093b81c55f","body":{"detail":"release_unconnected (now crates/clax-store/src/people.rs:2363) no longer releases a person who redeemed an invite (a hosted daemon's browser redeems one without a grant; 5274dba44) or who has a GitHub identity (dfe4b35d3). Store::grants_next_due (line 2109) now names an unredeemed invite's lapse, one second after its expires_at, so the sweep releases its person then rather than at the next periodic sweep (1fc405b97). The release still sets person = 0 and rights_json = NULL with no person.rights event, and the lapse itself records nothing: the record's concern stands at the moved lines.","kind":"comment","references":"05ca3c90a72b9254238c8d4ff6ac2fdff13d731d1a21261c0e67eac9642a67cd","summary":"Changed since recorded: fewer people are released, and a lapse is acted on when it happens; neither the lapse nor the release is recorded yet","tags":["review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/sessions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T16:19:13.450916Z","id":"2bc16a1ffb9ca8e43723b87ae31b78f9082230a6adaeacf7dcaa603c77088e1f","body":{"detail":"6704086a6 rewrote reaper_ends_only_idle_sessions_with_dead_or_unknown_pids (now crates/clax-store/src/sessions.rs:2297-2333) as the suggested fix asks: the store is test_util::store_with_clock(ManualClock::at(\"2026-09-01T10:00:00Z\")), the test advances the clock 301 s instead of std::thread::sleep(300 ms), and reap_sessions runs with a 300 s idle limit, so `fresh` is not idle however loaded the machine is. Not closed here: the record is main's.","kind":"comment","references":"9daba4912ee6d6dfc47850bd226691e02de2be5246e18c7cabb1f19500a18299","summary":"Fixed on this branch: the reaper test runs on an injected clock and sleeps no more; proposed close (reason fixed)","tags":["flaky-test","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T03:07:03.986308Z","id":"53d8fb26f896fee66590251760eb4e7e44df6ce88c874f26fb24b3422982111e","body":{"detail":"Copies of migrations 24 and 25 from 2026-10-10 (git log -S page_person -- crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs: e1b714b28, 827bc1568, 3e1ce3762, 4b6a1d656) add versions.page_person and comments.page_person, which the final migrations replace with versions.by_page/file_authors_json and page_authors. repair() does not drop or carry them: no code reads them, the meaning of their values does not map onto page_authors rows one for one, and only development homes of that week can hold them. Such a home keeps two dead nullable columns, so its schema differs from a new one's by them. tests/fixtures/old-migrations holds no fixture of that shape.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1481},"end":{"line":1535},"content_hash":"928042f66c850e8ea90b44e60bbd252daca90b7cf4434d3a220ab157eeaa8ac2"},"summary":"Migration 37's repair leaves comments.page_person and versions.page_person where an early multi-person build added them","tags":["migrations","revisit:a home made by a 2026-10-10 multi-person build is still in use","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T03:07:03.986467Z","id":"fa745f606c9055872b699176fe9818078c10186833a94c16971e0e79f18e59ec","body":{"detail":"Failure: a home whose user_version is 29 and whose migration 29 was 98b628173's device publishing (crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs blob c196df9e8, branch rust-int, 2026-10-14T01:08) fails Store::open with 'table device_codes already exists' when the current migration 30 runs. The next commit, b8015c192 two minutes later, renumbered it, so only a home opened by that one build is affected. Migration 37 cannot reach it; a fix would have to change migration 30 (CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS) or detect the shape before it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1114},"end":{"line":1130},"content_hash":"68c376ab25c5adbecd810ad5d5460206150cc8eea0ae13e01d8925b1b44388a5"},"summary":"A database left at schema 29 by rust-int commit 98b628173 fails migration 30 before migration 37 can repair it","tags":["migrations","revisit:a home made by rust-int commit 98b628173 is reported","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T03:07:03.986562Z","id":"5c74e449554814d7920430d1d7d493fea8fdd64a20534e25b32b25cb5cc1ec7f","body":{"detail":"rust-int commit c308495e6 (2026-10-14) made push_approvals without upto (NOT NULL, no default), so the table is rebuilt. No version is recorded for such a row; 0 approves none, where the artifact's current version could approve one the owner never saw. Only a local daemon writes push_approvals, so a hosted database has no such rows. Tested by migrations::tests::repair::migration_37_carries_inbox_items_and_push_approvals_through_their_rebuilds.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1346},"end":{"line":1351},"content_hash":"8e82eb74502c4778d5b82adb86e36b45a5abfb6246d88681ff24f0b686d20fcb"},"summary":"Migration 37 keeps a push_approvals row that lacks upto with upto = 0, so its push asks the owner again","tags":["migrations","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/engagement.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T18:56:07.897683Z","id":"28a9474386f523910274883c115bd15164bcd869f107033269adcd36951edcba","body":{"detail":"Store::note_delivery keeps delivered_written_at only for a comment with author_kind 'viewer', via_page = 0 and author_public_id equal to the session's person (else the owner's public ID). A page writing through the comments capability may do so without the person's input, so its time is left out; the delivery still places the question. Not taken: counting via_page comments by their author_public_id like hand-written ones.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":136},"end":{"line":143},"content_hash":"aa65147c5240be1bf3f96347a7648545424a0791a5cadd4bff56664d6da32391"},"summary":"A comment a page wrote as the person (via_page) is not the person's Clax activity","tags":["revisit:pages write comments only on the person's own action and those deliveries are suggested as the terminal wrongly","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/engagement.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T19:22:17.260933Z","id":"ada756fec31a27fb10d6cdc96be0ceee2c3ec8e9ac9e109187c996dee7dba619","body":{"detail":"Store::note_answer keeps the question's pulled_at, else closed_at, as delivered_written_at, so clax_core::surface::suggest weighs it against the last terminal prompt (crates/clax-server/src/routes/feedback.rs late_answers). Only the question's recipient, the session's person, can answer, skip or pull (Store::question_of in crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs owner_close), so it is their own act. It includes an answer through the token from no browser (answered_via cli), which is the person but not in a Clax tab.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":151},"end":{"line":174},"content_hash":"292cbdda1ba104c7e133fdce0b41b673c0f4a213b4bae9b2c921cb50d9540c58"},"summary":"An answer, skip or Ask me here handed over counts as the person's Clax activity at the time they acted; the path not taken lets it only place the suggestion, as a delivered comment by another author does","tags":["revisit:answers with answered_via cli become common, or the owner wants a delivery never to count as activity","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/engagement.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T19:41:40.494227Z","id":"753afb8fe5f0467633ea947700911537d845fadb18712600b7630c60b268e599","body":{"detail":"Store::note_delivery keeps delivered_written_at only for a comment with author_kind 'viewer', via_page = 0 and author_public_id equal to the session's person (else the owner's public ID). A page writing through the comments capability may do so without the person's input, so its time is left out; the delivery still places the question. Not taken: counting via_page comments by their author_public_id like hand-written ones.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":141},"end":{"line":148},"content_hash":"aa65147c5240be1bf3f96347a7648545424a0791a5cadd4bff56664d6da32391"},"summary":"A comment a page wrote as the person (via_page) is not the person's Clax activity","supersedes":"28a9474386f523910274883c115bd15164bcd869f107033269adcd36951edcba","tags":["revisit:pages write comments only on the person's own action and those deliveries are suggested as the terminal wrongly","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/engagement.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T19:41:40.517315Z","id":"84297a70fa901d940ed3dcee23ef49d3227940fd0c0ee18f6f5b08c8acb765f8","body":{"detail":"Store::note_answer keeps the question's pulled_at, else closed_at, as delivered_written_at, and what the person did as delivered_act, so clax_core::surface::suggest weighs it against the last terminal prompt (crates/clax-server/src/routes/feedback.rs late_answers). A question about no artifact (an inbox question) sets only the act and delivered_since_turn, leaving the last delivery's time and place. Only the question's recipient, the session's person, can answer, skip or pull (Store::question_of in crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs owner_close), so it is their own act. It includes an answer through the token from no browser (answered_via cli), which is the person but not in a Clax tab.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":162},"end":{"line":196},"content_hash":"eabddad981a8df370ada43c1e699e0491d2c7bccbdd43884610b9e9989e731e2"},"summary":"An answer, skip or Ask me here handed over counts as the person's Clax activity at the time they acted; the path not taken lets it only place the suggestion, as a delivered comment by another author does","supersedes":"ada756fec31a27fb10d6cdc96be0ceee2c3ec8e9ac9e109187c996dee7dba619","tags":["revisit:answers with answered_via cli become common, or the owner wants a delivery never to count as activity","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
